## Why This Is Asked

This question tests building a scalable, privacy-preserving, multi-tenant ML platform with end-to-end governance, not just a single model. It emphasizes per-tenant isolation, drift monitoring, fairness constraints, and safe rollout strategies in production.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant isolation and data governance
- Privacy-preserving techniques (DP/FL)
- Drift detection and alerting
- Fairness and per-tenant constraints
- Offline/online evaluation and canary rollouts
- Observability and rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
function driftScore(distA, distB) {
  // simplistic KL-divergence proxy
  let s = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < distA.length; i++) {
    const a = distA[i] + 1e-9, b = distB[i] + 1e-9;
    s += a * Math.log(a / b);
  }
  return s;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you design per-tenant feature schemas and a model registry?
- What latency/throughput targets and monitoring dashboards would you implement to catch regressions fast?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical domain adaptation for multimodal models under edge latency constraints; evaluates PEFT decisions, data strategy, and evaluation protocols.

## Key Concepts
- Multimodal alignment
- Domain adaptation with limited labels
- PEFT (Adapters/LoRA)
- Inference acceleration on edge
- Evaluation metrics for cross-domain retrieval

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: apply LoRA adapters to a pretrained transformer
const model = loadModel('fashion_multimodal_base');
const adapters = loadAdapters('fashion_lora');
model.applyAdapters(adapters);
model.train(fashionDataset, {
  loss: 'supervisedContrastive',
  batchSize: 32,
  epochs: 10
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses understanding of privacy-preserving, real-time ML systems that operate across devices and cloud infrastructure. It tests knowledge of multimodal processing, latency optimization, federated learning, and production ML lifecycle management.

## Key Concepts
- On-device inference with early-exit classifiers for sub-60ms latency
- Server-side multimodal fusion for ambiguous cases
- Federated learning with secure aggregation for privacy-preserving model updates
- Latency budgeting across device tiers and cloud GPUs
- Drift detection and model calibration
- Language-agnostic feature extraction

## Code Example
```javascript
// On-device early-exit classifier skeleton
async function moderateContent(input) {
  const preprocessed = await preprocess(input);
  const earlyExit = await runEarlyExitModel(preprocessed);

  if (earlyExit.confidence > 0.95) {
    return { decision: earlyExit.label, source: 'on-device' };
  }
  if (earlyExit.confidence > 0.7) {
    const encrypted = await encryptForServer(preprocessed);
    const serverResult = await sendToFusionModel(encrypted);
    return { decision: serverResult.label, source: 'server' };
  }
  return { decision: 'review', source: 'manual' };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale multilingual coverage beyond initial supported languages?
- How would you verify and audit privacy budgets (ε-differential privacy) in production?
- What is your strategy for handling emerging hate speech patterns and novel toxicity types?
